; The MCP server process. It is the only executable that links [pol_mcp], and
; the only file in the MCP tree allowed to perform I/O — the read/write loop
; lives here so every module it drives stays a function from values to values.

; Installed alongside `pol` as `pol-mcp`, so a machine that only ran
; `opam install pol` can point an MCP client at it with nothing else to fetch.

; ONE module on purpose. Dune wraps a multi-module executable as
; [Dune__exe__…], and this exe's main module has the same name as the library
; it links — so a second module here turns [Pol_mcp.Server] into an alias for
; the executable itself and the build stops. The generated [Version] therefore
; lives in the library next door, not beside this file.

(executable
 (name pol_mcp)
 (public_name pol-mcp)
 (package pol)
 (modules pol_mcp)
 (libraries pol_data pol_syntax pol_runtime pol_mcp pol_json pol_loadpath))
